---
description: Use this rules when asked to create handlers or endpoints
globs: 
alwaysApply: false
---

- The handlers should be created in /internal/server/handlers
- The request bodies and the validation should be in internal/requests
- The response types should be in internal/responses (hide any critical information such as passwords)
- Create comments to follow swaggo swag documentation for each endpoint handler
- create a type for swag (if needed) and put it in the responses folder
- run the swag command and finalizing to update the api documentation schema.
- use the users handler as a refrence 
- utalize helper functions from pkg/utils/utils if needed to convert db types, if you need to create other utils similar create it there.